# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Training data and model artifacts - never commit these.
#
# The rules above already keep everything under training_data/ out of git
# except the small vocabulary files in training_data/processed/vocabulary_analysis/.
# The patterns below also catch data written outside that directory (e.g. a
# custom --out-dir / --processed-dir) so a stray multi-GB file cannot be
# committed by accident.
#
# To get the data back:
#   python data_processing/download_rfam.py --stage prebuilt   # semRfam, ~2.2 GB
#   python data_processing/download_rfam.py --stage seed-all   # or rebuild locally
#   hf download MasterYster/yakRNA-Design yakRNA_110M.pt --local-dir checkpoints/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raw Rfam downloads and per-family alignments
*.sto
*.cm
*.cm.i1*
*.ssi
*.fa
*.fasta
*.fa.gz
Rfam.seed*
Rfam.cm*
Rfam.fa*
rfam2go*

# Tokenized dataset and its bulky intermediates (HDF5 is covered by *.h5 above)
semRfam*.h5
bert_ready_data.json
initial_sequence_extraction.json
family_lookup.json
family_splits.json
*_family_splits.json
GO_mappings.json

# Per-stage failure reports from download_rfam.py
*_failures.txt
